=== layout: one-panel

# Movie Night: Choose Our Movie

@body

- [*Movie Night*]{color=#24578F}: Tuesday, November 17
- Choose from *Our Times*, *Biosphere*, *Vesper*, and *The Animal Kingdom*.
- Vote after the four movie slides.

=== layout: movie-panel

# *Our Times (2025)*

@body

- Plot\: In 1966, married scientists Nora and H&#233;ctor invent a time machine that transports them to 2025. While Nora thrives in a world offering women greater opportunities in science, H&#233;ctor struggles to adapt, putting their marriage and careers to the test.
  - IMDb *5.4*,&#160;3.3k&#160;votes
  - RT&#160;audience\:&#160;&#127871;&#128078;&#160;48%
- Genre\: Science Fiction, Romance, Comedy
- Director\: Chava Cartas
- Run time\: 90 min
- *Original language*\: Spanish
- *Review Summary*\: Critics praised the film&#8217;s exploration of changing gender roles and its engaging performances, but found the writing uneven, with predictable conflicts and an unsatisfying conclusion.

@poster

![Our Times (2025) movie poster](assets/movie_choices/image_001.jpg)

=== layout: movie-panel

# *Biosphere (2023)*

@body

- Two men believe they are the last humans alive, surviving inside a sealed biosphere after an unexplained catastrophe. When their carefully maintained ecosystem begins to change, they face an unexpected biological challenge that could determine humanity&#8217;s future.
  - IMDb *5.5*,&#160;3.3k&#160;votes | Metacritic\:&#160;&#129000;&#160;59
  - RT&#160;critics\:&#160;&#127813;&#160;80% | RT&#160;audience\:&#160;&#127871;&#160;60%
- Genre\: Comedy, Drama, Science Fiction, Fantasy
- Director\: Mel Eslyn
- Run time\: 106 min
- *Review Summary*\: Critics praised the chemistry between the two leads, quirky humor, and unusual scientific premise, but some found the story repetitive, poorly paced, and ultimately unsatisfying.

@poster

![Biosphere (2023) movie poster](assets/movie_choices/image_002.jpg)

=== layout: movie-panel

# *Vesper (2022)*

@body

- After Earth&#8217;s ecosystems collapse, a 13-year-old girl uses her skills in genetic engineering to survive while caring for her paralyzed father. When she encounters a mysterious stranger, she discovers an opportunity that could change their future.
  - IMDb *6.0*,&#160;28k&#160;votes | Metacritic\:&#160;&#129001;&#160;70
  - RT&#160;critics\:&#160;&#127813;&#127942;&#160;91% | RT&#160;audience\:&#160;&#127871;&#128078;&#160;58%
- Genre\: Science Fiction, Drama, Adventure, Fantasy
- Director\: Kristina Buo&#382;yt&#279;, Bruno Samper
- Run time\: 112 min
- *Review Summary*\: Critics praised the stunning visuals, imaginative biological world, and intelligent ideas, but found the story slow-moving and less compelling than its impressive setting.

@poster

![Vesper (2022) movie poster](assets/movie_choices/image_003.jpg)

=== layout: movie-panel

# *The Animal Kingdom (2023)*

@body

- A mysterious condition is transforming humans into animal-like creatures. As society struggles to respond, a father and his teenage son search for their missing wife and mother, who is undergoing the transformation herself.
  - IMDb *6.7*,&#160;12k&#160;votes | Metacritic\:&#160;&#129001;&#160;69
  - RT&#160;critics\:&#160;&#127813;&#127942;&#160;83% | RT&#160;audience\:&#160;&#127871;&#160;75%
- Genre\: Adventure, Drama, Science Fiction
- Director\: Thomas Cailley
- Run time\: 127 min
- *Original language*\: French
- *Review Summary*\: Critics praised the strong performances, emotional storytelling, and imaginative creature designs, but some felt the film explored its intriguing scientific and social themes only superficially.

@poster

![The Animal Kingdom (2023) movie poster](assets/movie_choices/image_004.jpg)

